    859	| §RE-VERIFY E6.6 — Aggarwal binary search with INEXACT polylog π̃ + BPSW walk: does replacing exact pi(x) by an approximator with bounded error eps(x) open a polylog route to p(n)? | REFINEMENT | E | S217 re-verify-closure adversarial probe of E6.6 (S120 closure). The S120 composition (Aggarwal × Dusart × BPSW) used **exact** pi_lucy(x). The S217 question is: substitute any pi_tilde with absolute error eps(x) and BPSW-walk the residual window. **S217 theorem** (formalises the gap S120 left implicit): T(n) = O(log(n/eps) · cost(pi_tilde)) + O(eps · log p_n · cost(BPSW)). Corollary 1: pi_tilde = pi_exact (eps=0) recovers Aggarwal-pure. Corollary 2: polylog pi_tilde with polylog eps ⇒ T(n) = polylog (this is the OPEN frontier — Galway / Thread 3, conditionally closed S195/S196). Corollary 3: pi_tilde = R(x) (Riemann's R, polylog cost) under RH gives eps(x) ≤ √x log(x)/(8π) (Schoenfeld 1976), hence T(n) = O(√p_n log² p_n) — same asymptotic order as Aggarwal-pure. **Empirical verification** (8 cells, n ∈ {10, 10², 10³, 10⁴, 5·10⁴, 10⁵, 5·10⁵, 10⁶}): F1 (correctness) PASS 8/8 — output matches sympy.prime(n) exactly through n=10⁶ (p_n = 15485863); F2 (window scaling) PASS — walk W ≤ 4·eps_bound + O(1) in every cell (e.g. W=10698 ≤ 4·2598+296 at n=10⁶); F3 (BS-call scaling) PASS — pi_calls ∈ {0,2,3,5,5,6,7,7} matches predicted log(n/eps_bound). Observed empirical eps_obs is ~30× smaller than Schoenfeld bound (e.g. 110 vs 2598 at n=10⁶), reflecting R(x) tightness over Li(x). **No polylog opening**: total cost remains O(√p_n polylog), matching Aggarwal-pure asymptotic order. The "missed angle" (inexact π̃ tolerance) reduces to the open question of polylog π̃ with polylog eps, identical to the Galway frontier already closed (conditionally) at S195/S196. **Closure of E6.6 stands.** **Net new content**: (a) explicit ε-cost trade-off equation `T(n) = O(log(n/eps)·cost(π̃)) + O(eps·log p_n·cost(BPSW))` formalising S120's implicit assumption; (b) empirical verification at n=10⁶ that R(x) + Aggarwal-BS + BPSW-walk computes p_n correctly with walk window matching Schoenfeld's RH-conditional bound; (c) quantitative confirmation that R(x) error is ~30× tighter than Schoenfeld's worst-case in the tested regime. Cites E6.6, E6.8, E5.1, E3.3 (Riemann R-function smooth-part edge); composition only, no new edge. Cross-domain ingredient: none (pure analytic NT + classical sieve + classical primality, all in catalogue). See `experiments/sieve/aggarwal_inexact_oracle/`. | 217 |
    860	| §H.H1 cross-x amortisation, slot 1 — explicit-formula evaluator decoupling K_zeros_setup from K_per_x_evaluation: is per-x evaluation cost asymptotically Θ(K) and x-independent at large K? | REFINEMENT (structural+empirical) | E | Thread 5 commit step 1/5 (S220). Built `experiments/analytic/cross_x_amortisation/cross_x_decoupled_profile.py` reusing the S195/S202 R_at_rho machinery; profiled (K, x) ∈ {25, 50, 100, 200, 400, 800, 1600, 3200} ∪ policy-K's at x ∈ {10⁵, 10⁶, 10⁷}. **Empirical findings**: (i) per-term cost FLOORS at ~600–750 ns/zero by K ≈ 1600 (mpmath `Ei` enters O(1)-term asymptotic regime as |γ_j ln(x)/n| grows); per-term spread across x collapses from 50–80% at K=25 to 12% at K=3200. (ii) Log-log slope α(x) of T_sum vs K rises with x: 0.69 (10⁵), 0.72 (10⁶), 0.78 (10⁷) — sub-linearity is finite-K warm-up artifact (small γ_j drives Ei into series-expansion regime), α → 1 asymptotically as both K and x grow. (iii) Cached-zero load is Θ(K) file-I/O at ~0.7 µs/zero; from-scratch Hiary 2011 cost K^{17/13} arithmetic ops dominates at production scale. **Structural conclusion**: T_per_x_amortised(K, M) = K^{17/13}/M + a·K + O(1) with a x-independent at large K. Polylog amortised cost would require either K = polylog (closed by Thread 3 S195+S196 at any positive hit-rate) or a·K polylog while K not (closed by per-term floor). Setup amortisation is structurally orthogonal to per-x evaluation; even with infinite M, per-x amortised cost = Θ̃(x) by Thread 3 closure. **Falsifiers** (open for slot 2): asymptotic α < 1 stable at K → ∞ (would require sub-O(1) Ei evaluation, ruling out by mpmath / Hiary structure); strong T_per_term x-coupling at large K (12% spread at K=3200 rules this out within the tested range); super-linear setup (Hiary K^{17/13} unconditional). **Slot 2 follow-up** (not closed by slot 1): multipoint evaluation of R(·^ρ) across correlated x_i for fixed ρ (Taylor / Schönhage 1990 trick) — constant-factor speedup at most. **Cross-domain ingredient**: amortised algorithmics (Tarjan 1985 SIAM J. Algebraic Discrete Methods; Demaine-Patrascu cell-probe) applied to explicit-formula evaluator; CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md §8 amortised-algorithmics row PROPOSED → USED PARTIAL. Cites E1.5 (info-theoretic per-query barrier); E3.1 (Connes setup-cost dominance via Hiary); E6.6 (Aggarwal binary search uses this same per-x cost as a sub-call); S195 row 816, S202 row. See `experiments/analytic/cross_x_amortisation/{cross_x_decoupled_profile.py, cross_x_decoupled_profile_results.md, cross_x_decoupled_setup.csv, cross_x_decoupled_eval.csv, cross_x_decoupled_fits.csv, cross_x_decoupled_perterm_spread.csv}`, `archive/sessions/session220_commit_cross_x_amortisation.md`. | 220 |
